5. Live Execution Loop & Governance Rules


A. Live Hot-Path Rules

1. Strict Gold-Only Reads: The execution engine reads only from Redis Gold keys. It never queries Bronze/Silver storage or invokes heavy Python/Pandas rolling calculations on the hot path.
2. Kite Rate-Limit Token Bucket: Wrap order routing in a rate limiter enforcing ≤ 8 orders/sec (buffer under Kite’s 10/sec cap), ≤ 350 orders/min, and < 20 modifications per order ID (auto-cancel/replace at modification #20).
3. Cross-Asset Regime Consumption:
	• Normal / Elevated IV: Scale cash-equity and naked option lot sizes inversely to gold_options_regime.atm_iv and widen ATR stops using expected straddle move.
	• Hard Gate Trigger: Block all new long cash/short-put entries if India VIX > 24, intraday VIX spikes > 15%, or front-week IV enters steep backwardation ahead of RBI/Budget events.

B. Staleness & Circuit-Breaker Fallbacks

Every Gold artifact carries published_at_utc and source_tick_utc. Before firing any order, the live loop checks now_utc - source_tick_utc:
• Fresh (< 2s for tick features / < 65s for 1m bars): Execute normally.
• Degraded (2s–10s lag): Block new entries; allow resting SL/TP exit orders only.
• Stale / Disconnected (> 10s lag or WebSocket drop): Trigger kill switch—cancel all pending limit orders, halt strategy loop, and alert immediately.

6. Backtest & Validation Standards

• Coverage: 2017–2026 (9+ years) of 1-minute cash/index bars across point-in-time NIFTY 500 constituents (survivorship-bias-free) + 2021–2026 (5+ years) of 1-minute option chains (archived daily from your Bronze layer going forward, backfilled via historical NSE tick vendors).
• Statistical Thresholds: Minimum 100–150 independent trades per regime bucket (Low-IV Trend, High-IV Mean-Reversion, Expiry/Event) before live deployment.
• Latency SLAs: Capture latency < 50 ms (p95); End-to-End Decision Latency (Tick → Kite Order API call) < 150 ms (p99); Throughput burst capacity ≥ 200 decisions/sec at 09:15 IST open.
