2. Multi-Process Topology & IPC Boundaries

Isolate your platform into 4 independent OS processes so a heavy backtest or garbage-collection pause never blocks live order execution:
1. Process 1: kite_ingestor (Bronze Writer)
	• Connects to Kite WebSockets (KiteTicker), pushes raw ticks into a Redis Stream (stream:ticks:nse, stream:ticks:nfo) for real-time consumers, and buffers ticks in RAM to flush immutable Parquet chunks to data/bronze/YYYY-MM-DD/ every 60 seconds.
2. Process 2: silver_normalizer (Silver Writer)
	• Consumes from Redis Streams, aggregates 1-second/1-minute bars, computes Black-76 option Greeks via vectorized NumPy/Polars, and maintains rolling intraday state in an in-memory DuckDB instance. Persists finalized EOD Silver tables to data/silver/ after 15:35 IST.
3. Process 3: gold_publisher (Gold Writer)
	• Computes NIFTY 500 breadth, options regime (IVR, GEX, PCR), and watchlist features. Publishes latest state to Redis Hashes (gold:regime:nifty, gold:features:{token}) with an atomic published_at_utc timestamp, and logs 1-minute snapshots to data/gold/ for historical replay.
4. Process 4: execution_router (Gold Reader & Order Sender)
	• Runs the live strategy loop. Reads exclusively from Redis Gold keys (zero disk I/O), verifies staleness TTL (< 2s), applies Kite rate-limit buckets (≤ 8 orders/sec), and sends orders.

3. Why This Beats SQLite / Single-File Databases for Multi-Process Trading

• Eliminates database is locked errors: SQLite and single-file DuckDB allow only one writer process at a time and choke under concurrent high-frequency tick writes + analytical queries. Separating Redis (live multi-process IPC) from Immutable Parquet + DuckDB (analytical queries) removes all lock contention.
• Zero-Copy Analytical Reads: Polars and DuckDB natively memory-map (mmap) partitioned Parquet files. You can run a 9-year backtest in a 5th process (research_worker) scanning millions of Silver option rows in seconds without touching the live trading processes.
• Crash Recovery & Replay: If silver_normalizer or gold_publisher crashes mid-session, it simply replays today's Redis Stream (or today's data/bronze/ Parquet files) from 09:15 IST and reconstructs exact state in under 2 seconds.

